==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|get with the programme}} {{qualifier|UK}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-get with the program.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|get<,,got,gotten> with the program|head=[[get with]] [[the]] [[program]]}}

# {{lb|en|US|idiomatic|informal}} To become [[organized]], [[current]], or [[aware]].
#: {{ux|en|When the student was behind on his vocabulary, the teacher said, "get with the program!"}}
# {{lb|en|US|idiomatic|informal}} To work productively toward the objective of a shared enterprise, especially after the objective or the environment has changed.
#: {{ux|en|Though natural gas prices dropped, the folks doing solar didn't '''get with the program'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2017-11-07|author=Aja Romano|title=The unlikely breakout star of Stranger Things 2 is unlikelier babysitter Steve Harrington|journal={{w|Vox (website)|Vox}}|url=https://www.vox.com/culture/2017/10/30/16569330/dad-steve-harrington-stranger-things-2-memes|passage=In the first season of ''Stranger Things'', no character was more extra than Steve Harrington — Nancy Wheeler’s frequently possessive, largely confused, often douchey boyfriend. Though he eventually '''got with the program''' and helped fight some monsters, he wasn’t exactly what you’d call the pick of the litter.}}
# {{lb|en|US|idiomatic|informal}} To comply with the norms of a social group, especially a shared enterprise; to comply with the [[accepted]] or [[prevail]]ing way of doing things.
#: {{ux|en|Dude, '''get with the program'''! We don't do casual Fridays any more.}}

